      ":question/problem": "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [0,1]\u2286{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-4x{y}^{2}-x+6{y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[1,\\,0]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration. Round the answer for ${x}_{1}$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n| $[$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$ | {{field-2}} | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-3}} | $-8$ | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n\n| ${x}_{1}=[$ | $1$ | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-4}} |  |  |"
